description:
Sample-audit accepted corpus gold **before** scheduling the ~750-annotation adjudication workstreams.

This is a trust check, not a migration. Read a stratified sample of accepted annotations across packets and layers (mentions, data items, components, flows). Record:

- mislabels (concept does not match evidence);
- source-token-only identities treated as concepts;
- type/subtype errors;
- duplicate or collapsed entities;
- flow endpoints that are not graph nodes;
- any packet whose error rate is high enough that the packet should not be migrated.

Do not start KDATAP-a0e80b (data-item adjudication) or KDATAP-8e7756 (flow regold) until this reports.

If the sample error rate is high, **stop and escalate**. The answer is probably to shrink the corpus to packets that earn trust, not to migrate 1,792 annotations. That is a scope decision, not an engineering one.

Do not retune detectors. Do not rewrite gold in this task except to record the audit notes. Writers cannot self-accept the audit.

Definition of done: sample method, packet/layer coverage, error counts, and a go/no-go recommendation are recorded on this issue. Adjudication stays blocked until a human accepts the recommendation.
